From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebberich <sebberich@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] Mobile: Fix Bluetooth nearby connections between two
 phones

Found in the first two-phone test: the legacy advertisement was too large
(47 > 31 bytes) so only the coded-PHY set was visible, connects then used
1M PHY (status 133/147), every scan hit started another connectGatt and
old GATT clients were never closed, both phones connected as central, and
frames arriving before the session existed were dropped.

- Advertise data with the service UUID, token and a 4-byte role nonce in
  the scan response; coded PHY only with the new experimental
  "Bluetooth Long Range" setting.
- Only the phone with the smaller nonce connects; one connect at a time,
  10 s timeout, close on failure, per-peer backoff, scan paused while
  connecting.
- A link is ready only after MTU and notification subscription; frames
  that arrive earlier are buffered; links keyed by role and address.
- Session messages are handled one at a time in arrival order; pushes
  after stop() no longer reject unhandled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015mATJ5zDWtHUm4X7vhb9u2

